{
  "dom_id": "step-q118850",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14247585/assets/0a2f45da66edebc2c565b36472648c76421a33513fb51c6a26e79e7a551b526e.png)\n\nDetermine the height of the rectangular solid above given that its volume is $90\\,{\\text{ft}}^{3}.$",
  "worked_solution": "We can find the volume $V$ of the rectangular prism using the formula\n\n$$\nV=lwh,\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length, $w$ is the width, and $h$ is the height of the solid.\n\nSubstituting\n\n$$\nV=90,\\,l=3,\\,w=5\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}90 & =3\\cdot 5\\cdot h \\\\ 90 & =15h \\\\ h & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the height is $6\\,\\text{ft}.$",
